# Cindy on Fedora Linux: Installation and Update Guide

This guide documents my experience installing and updating [Cindy](https://cindy.app/) on **Fedora 44 Workstation with GNOME**.

The process is divided into two parts:

- **Part 1 – Initial Installation:** Installing and launching Cindy 0.1.120 by extracting the official Debian package.
- **Part 2 – Update and Migration:** Moving from the manually extracted installation to Cindy 0.1.121 using the official managed per-user installer.

> **Tested environment:** Fedora 44 Workstation, GNOME, x86_64  
> **Initial version:** 0.1.120  
> **Updated version:** 0.1.121  
> **Installation method:** Managed per-user installation  
> **Result:** Successfully launched on my system.

This is a community-contributed installation report based on my own testing. It does not imply that Fedora is an officially supported or fully tested distribution.

## Official Documentation

Before proceeding, check Cindy's official Linux installation guide for the latest instructions:

- [Cindy Linux installation guide](https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/blob/main/docs/linux.md)
- [Cindy website](https://cindy.app/)

The commands and checksum in this guide document the specific versions used during my testing. They should not be assumed to apply unchanged to future releases.

