# Final Result

I successfully installed and launched Cindy 0.1.120 on Fedora 44 Workstation by extracting the official Debian package.

When the built-in updater rejected the manually extracted installation, I migrated to Cindy 0.1.121 using the official managed per-user installer bundled with the verified package.

The new installation launched successfully and was registered in the GNOME application menu. I also resolved the duplicate launcher caused by my earlier manual setup.

This guide documents what worked on my Fedora system. Other Fedora configurations and future Cindy releases may require different steps.

For the latest installation instructions, always consult the [official Cindy Linux installation guide](https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/blob/main/docs/linux.md).
